        body: "<p>Testosterone can be delivered in several forms - injections, topical gels, creams and long-acting pellets. Each has trade-offs in convenience, cost and how steady the resulting levels are. Our overview of the <a href=\"/trt/articles/types-of-trt\">types of TRT</a> compares them in detail.</p><p>Whatever the format, good care includes <strong>ongoing monitoring</strong>. Follow-up bloodwork checks that testosterone is in a healthy range and watches for side effects such as a rising red blood cell count. Depending on your history, a clinician may also monitor estradiol, PSA and prostate health. TRT is not a set-and-forget therapy.</p>",
